# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build context
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The ONLY thing this Dockerfile reads from the build context is
# docker_selfcheck.py -- the single `COPY` at the bottom. The app itself is
# cloned from GitHub and every dependency is fetched over the network, so
# nothing else needs to be sent.
#
# The container entrypoint is deliberately NOT a context file: it is generated
# inside the Dockerfile from a quoted heredoc, so there is nothing here to
# re-admit for it. Do not add a `!docker-entrypoint.sh` line -- there is no such
# file in the repo, and a whitelist entry for a missing file is a silent no-op
# that looks like it does something.
#
# Without this file the context is ~14 GB (`runs/` alone), which BuildKit has to
# hash and transfer on every single build. It also means `.env` -- which holds
# HF_TOKEN, GITHUB_TOKEN and CLOUDFLARED_TOKEN -- gets uploaded to whatever
# builder is in use.
#
# So: ignore everything, then re-admit the one file that is actually used.
*
!docker_selfcheck.py
